rrentUser dependency definition or an equivalent upstream observation, but it is not decisive under the question's explicit entry premise.","facts":[{"id":"f-entry","kind":"entry","statement":"The declared GET item endpoint is handled by read_item and accepts an item id.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-dcbab1685696c702","startLine":48,"endLine":49}]},{"id":"f-principal-binding","kind":"binding","statement":"At handler entry, the principal is represented by the current_user parameter annotated as CurrentUser; the annotation's implementation is not shown here.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-dcbab1685696c702","startLine":49,"endLine":49}]},{"id":"f-current-user-import","kind":"binding","statement":"CurrentUser is imported from the dependency module, but this crop does not expose its upstream authentication or active-user semantics.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-dcbab1685696c702","startLine":7,"endLine":7}]},{"id":"f-resource-binding","kind":"binding","statement":"The protected resource is bound by loading Item with the handler's id through the session.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-dcbab1685696c702","startLine":53,"endLine":53}]},{"id":"f-existence-condition","kind":"condition","statement":"A failed resource lookup produces a 404 before authorization; the task premise that the item exists makes this path inapplicable.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-dcbab1685696c702","startLine":53,"endLine":55}]},{"id":"f-authorization-control","kind":"control","statement":"The strongest visible authorization control denies only when the caller is not a superuser and the item's owner id differs from the caller's id, so superuser status overrides the ownership mismatch for this read.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-dcbab1685696c702","startLine":56,"endLine":57}]},{"id":"f-read-effect","kind":"effect","statement":"If neither the missing-item nor permission exception is raised, the handler returns the item as the read effect.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-dcbab1685696c702","startLine":58